{"step_index":67,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-05T22:36:17Z","input_tokens":2075,"cache_read_tokens":100131,"output_tokens":4846,"thinking":"The MikroTik configuration shows `ether1` as the internet input (WAN) and a `bridge-LAN` comprising ports `ether2` through `ether5`, assigned to the `192.168.15.0/24` network. The gateway is `192.168.15.1`. This network information will be crucial for understanding the overall network setup.\n\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nNetwork configuration details were examined to determine the available methods for managing bandwidth.  Multiple approaches emerged for assigning specific bandwidth tiers to network clients, including DHCP lease configuration and address-list based rules. Address-list-based methods with firewall mangling and queue tree were identified as a streamlined option.\n\n\nPPPoE and Hotspot profiles for different bandwidth tiers (5, 10, 20, 30, and 40 Mbps) are being created to support connections from devices like LiteBeam M5/PowerBeam M5.  The script will ensure FastTrack is disabled in the firewall to enable proper speed limiting via Simple Queues and Queue Trees.  Finally, the ready-to-use configuration file will be saved in two specified locations.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# ==============================================================================\n# PLANTILLA 06: PAQUETES DE INTERNET DE 5, 10, 20, 30 Y 40 MEGAS EN MIKROTIK\n# Compatible con RouterOS v6 y v7 (Red 192.168.15.x, Antenas Ubiquiti y PPPoE)\n# ==============================================================================\n# QUÉ HACE ESTE SCRIPT:\n# 1. Desactiva FastTrack en el Firewall (si está activo, las colas no limitan).\n# 2. Crea los Tipos de Cola PCQ (Per Connection Queue) para 5M, 10M, 20M, 30M y 40M\n#    para que cada cliente reciba exactamente su paquete de forma individual.\n# 3. Crea las Simple Queues para controlar clientes por IP fija o por rangos en\n#    tu red 192.168.15.x:\n#      - PAQUETE  5 MEGAS ( 5M Bajada /  5M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.50  - 192.168.15.89\n#      - PAQUETE 10 MEGAS (10M Bajada / 10M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.90  - 192.168.15.129\n#      - PAQUETE 20 MEGAS (20M Bajada / 20M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.130 - 192.168.15.169\n#      - PAQUETE 30 MEGAS (30M Bajada / 30M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.170 - 192.168.15.209\n#      - PAQUETE 40 MEGAS (40M Bajada / 40M Subida) -> Rango 192.168.15.210 - 192.168.15.250\n# 4. Incluye plantillas individuales por IP (con Ráfaga/Burst opcional) y también\n#    los 5 Perfiles PPPoE listos por si autenticas antenas LiteBeam/PowerBeam.\n# ==============================================================================\n\n{\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PASO 1: ASEGURAR QUE FASTTRACK ESTÉ DESACTIVADO PARA QUE LAS COLAS FUNCIONEN\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n/ip firewall filter remove [find action=\"fasttrack-connection\"]\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PASO 2: CREAR COLAS INTELIGENTES PCQ (CADA IP DENTRO DEL PAQUETE RECIBE SU VELOCIDAD)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n/queue type remove [find name~\"PCQ_PAQUETE_\"]\n\n# --- PCQ 5 MEGAS ---\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_5M_DOWN\" kind=pcq pcq-rate=5M pcq-classifier=dst-address pcq-dst-address-mask=32\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_5M_UP\"   kind=pcq pcq-rate=5M pcq-classifier=src-address pcq-src-address-mask=32\n\n# --- PCQ 10 MEGAS ---\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_10M_DOWN\" kind=pcq pcq-rate=10M pcq-classifier=dst-address pcq-dst-address-mask=32\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_10M_UP\"   kind=pcq pcq-rate=10M pcq-classifier=src-address pcq-src-address-mask=32\n\n# --- PCQ 20 MEGAS ---\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_20M_DOWN\" kind=pcq pcq-rate=20M pcq-classifier=dst-address pcq-dst-address-mask=32\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_20M_UP\"   kind=pcq pcq-rate=20M pcq-classifier=src-address pcq-src-address-mask=32\n\n# --- PCQ 30 MEGAS ---\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_30M_DOWN\" kind=pcq pcq-rate=30M pcq-classifier=dst-address pcq-dst-address-mask=32\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_30M_UP\"   kind=pcq pcq-rate=30M pcq-classifier=src-address pcq-src-address-mask=32\n\n# --- PCQ 40 MEGAS ---\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_40M_DOWN\" kind=pcq pcq-rate=40M pcq-classifier=dst-address pcq-dst-address-mask=32\n/queue type add name=\"PCQ_PAQUETE_40M_UP\"   kind=pcq pcq-rate=40M pcq-classifier=src-address pcq-src-address-mask=32\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PASO 3: CREAR LOS 5 PAQUETES EN \"SIMPLE QUEUES\" POR RANGOS DE IP (192.168.15.x)\n# (Cualquier antena o cliente que pongas en ese rango toma el paquete al instante)\n# Nota: En MikroTik el formato es Subida/Bajada (Upload/Download).\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n/queue simple remove [find name~\"PAQUETE_\"]\n\n# 1. PAQUETE DE 5 MEGAS (5 Mbps Subida / 5 Mbps Bajada por cada cliente)\n/queue simple add name=\"01_PAQUETE_05_MEGAS\" \\\n    target=192.168.15.50-192.168.15.89 \\\n    max-limit=100M/100M \\\n    queue=PCQ_PAQUETE_5M_UP/PCQ_PAQUETE_5M_DOWN \\\n    comment=\"PAQUETE 5 MEGAS por cliente (IPs: 192.168.15.50 al .89)\"\n\n# 2. PAQUETE DE 10 MEGAS (10 Mbps Subida / 10 Mbps Bajada por cada cliente)\n/queue simple add name=\"02_PAQUETE_10_MEGAS\" \\\n    target=192.168.15.90-192.168.15.129 \\\n    max-limit=200M/200M \\\n    queue=PCQ_PAQUETE_10M_UP/PCQ_PAQUETE_10M_DOWN \\\n    comment=\"PAQUETE 10 MEGAS por cliente (IPs: 192.168.15.90 al .129)\"\n\n# 3. PAQUETE DE 20 MEGAS (20 Mbps Subida / 20 Mbps Bajada por cada cliente)\n/queue simple add name=\"03_PAQUETE_20_MEGAS\" \\\n    target=192.168.15.130-192.168.15.169 \\\n    max-limit=300M/300M \\\n    queue=PCQ_PAQUETE_20M_UP/PCQ_PAQUETE_20M_DOWN \\\n    comment=\"PAQUETE 20 MEGAS por cliente (IPs: 192.168.15.130 al .169)\"\n\n# 4. PAQUETE DE 30 MEGAS (30 Mbps Subida / 30 Mbps Bajada por cada cliente)\n/queue simple add name=\"04_PAQUETE_30_MEGAS\" \\\n    target=192.168.15.170-192.168.15.209 \\\n    max-limit=500M/500M \\\n    queue=PCQ_PAQUETE_30M_UP/PCQ_PAQUETE_30M_DOWN \\\n    comment=\"PAQUETE 30 MEGAS por cliente (IPs: 192.168.15.170 al .209)\"\n\n# 5. PAQUETE DE 40 MEGAS (40 Mbps Subida / 40 Mbps Bajada por cada cliente)\n/queue simple add name=\"05_PAQUETE_40_MEGAS\" \\\n    target=192.168.15.210-192.168.15.250 \\\n    max-limit=600M/600M \\\n    queue=PCQ_PAQUETE_40M_UP/PCQ_PAQUETE_40M_DOWN \\\n    comment=\"PAQUETE 40 MEGAS por cliente (IPs: 192.168.15.210 al .250)\"\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PASO 4: PLANTILLAS DE COLAS INDIVIDUALES POR CLIENTE (PARA COPIAR O ACTIVAR EN WINBOX)\n# Se crean deshabilitadas (disabled=yes) como molde en Winbox -> Queues -> Simple Queues.\n# Solo haz doble clic, cambia la IP (ej. 192.168.15.10), pon el nombre del cliente y actívala.\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n/queue simple add name=\"PLANTILLA_CLIENTE_05_MEGAS\" target=192.168.15.251 max-limit=5M/5M \\\n    burst-limit=7M/7M burst-threshold=4M/4M burst-time=8s/8s disabled=yes \\\n    comment=\"Molde individual 5 Megas (con rafaga a 7M al abrir paginas)\"\n\n/queue simple add name=\"PLANTILLA_CLIENTE_10_MEGAS\" target=192.168.15.252 max-limit=10M/10M \\\n    burst-limit=14M/14M burst-threshold=8M/8M burst-time=8s/8s disabled=yes \\\n    comment=\"Molde individual 10 Megas (con rafaga a 14M al abrir paginas)\"\n\n/queue simple add name=\"PLANTILLA_CLIENTE_20_MEGAS\" target=192.168.15.253 max-limit=20M/20M \\\n    burst-limit=25M/25M burst-threshold=16M/16M burst-time=8s/8s disabled=yes \\\n    comment=\"Molde individual 20 Megas (con rafaga a 25M al abrir paginas)\"\n\n/queue simple add name=\"PLANTILLA_CLIENTE_30_MEGAS\" target=192.168.15.254 max-limit=30M/30M \\\n    burst-limit=38M/38M burst-threshold=25M/25M burst-time=8s/8s disabled=yes \\\n    comment=\"Molde individual 30 Megas (con rafaga a 38M al abrir paginas)\"\n\n/queue simple add name=\"PLANTILLA_CLIENTE_40_MEGAS\" target=192.168.15.250 max-limit=40M/40M \\\n    burst-limit=50M/50M burst-threshold=32M/32M burst-time=8s/8s disabled=yes \\\n    comment=\"Molde individual 40 Megas (con rafaga a 50M al abrir paginas)\"\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PASO 5: PERFILES PPPoE DE 5, 10, 20, 30 Y 40 MEGAS (EN \"PPP -> PROFILES\")\n# Listos por si conectas tus antenas LiteBeam M5 / PowerBeam M5 mediante PPPoE.\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n/ppp profile remove [find name~\"PAQUETE_\"]\n\n/ppp profile add name=\"PAQUETE_05_MEGAS\" local-address=192.168.15.1 remote-address=pool-15 \\\n    dns-server=1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8 rate-limit=\"5M/5M\" only-one=yes change-tcp-mss=yes \\\n    comment=\"Paquete PPPoE 5 Megas Simetricos\"\n\n/ppp profile add name=\"PAQUETE_10_MEGAS\" local-address=192.168.15.1 remote-address=pool-15 \\\n    dns-server=1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8 rate-limit=\"10M/10M\" only-one=yes change-tcp-mss=yes \\\n    comment=\"Paquete PPPoE 10 Megas Simetricos\"\n\n/ppp profile add name=\"PAQUETE_20_MEGAS\" local-address=192.168.15.1 remote-address=pool-15 \\\n    dns-server=1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8 rate-limit=\"20M/20M\" only-one=yes change-tcp-mss=yes \\\n    comment=\"Paquete PPPoE 20 Megas Simetricos\"\n\n/ppp profile add name=\"PAQUETE_30_MEGAS\" local-address=192.168.15.1 remote-address=pool-15 \\\n    dns-server=1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8 rate-limit=\"30M/30M\" only-one=yes change-tcp-mss=yes \\\n    comment=\"Paquete PPPoE 30 Megas Simetricos\"\n\n/ppp profile add name=\"PAQUETE_40_MEGAS\" local-address=192.168.15.1 remote-address=pool-15 \\\n    dns-server=1.1.1.1,8.8.8.8 rate-limit=\"40M/40M\" only-one=yes change-tcp-mss=yes \\\n    comment=\"Paquete PPPoE 40 Megas Simetricos\"\n}\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\microtik\\microtik\\00_Plantillas_RSC_Listas_Para_Usar\\06_paquetes_internet_5_10_20_30_40_megas.rsc"}}]}
